    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d591">

                <pb facs="0586" n="1320" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1320"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-08"><hi rendition="#italic">October 8,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Said Pasha, former foreign minister, reappointed. Consul of the United States at
                    Beirut reports activity of revolutionary leaders in interior, and that
                    missionaries dread being assassinated by revolutionists, who hope thus to bring
                    odium on the Turks. They also fear massacre by the Turks. My demand for orders
                    to all civil and military chiefs in all provinces for protection of Americans
                    has been renewed. Still dread the effect of recent events here on remote
                    provinces. * * * The Armenian churches have been filled for a week by Armenians
                    who refuse to leave, whether from apprehension or because revolutionary leaders
                    require it as an object lesson to influence Christian powers, opinions differ.
                    Order seems restored, but all Armenian business houses are closed under
                    instructions from Armenian committee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
